{"card_or_mechanic": "The Necrobloom", "contract_id": "card.The%20Necrobloom.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "10a9991f8d2a98fa635a7f703d5f79b0f316c17274e6afc4efc31851d943089b", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--c1e5473fdd48.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition.", "oracle_id": "b981af39-4ee6-4fbc-9a89-618dcad9dfbf", "oracle_text_sha256": "1d25c2af5439699d977cab605396630d6bcee1988be76807233ac201fc1bc49e", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "", "question": "Landfall with seven or more differently named lands in your graveyard: does the Zombie replace the Plant or add to it, when is the seven-names condition checked, does the entering land count, and do two lands entering give two triggers?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["614.15", "614.6", "608.2h", "603.4", "603.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "One token per trigger: the 'instead' is a self-replacement effect of the resolving ability (614.15), so the Plant never happens when the Zombie is created (614.6). The seven-different-names condition is not an intervening if (603.4); it is checked as the effect is applied, on resolution (608.2h), and the entering land counts."}, {"cr_citations": ["614.1a", "614.15", "603.4", "608.2h", "603.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "One token per trigger: the Zombie instead of the Plant is a self-replacement within the resolving ability (614.15). The condition is not an intervening if (603.4); it is checked only on resolution (608.2h), and the entering land counts if it is in the graveyard by then. Two lands entering are two triggers, each checked separately (603.2c)."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "The Necrobloom", "contract_id": "card.The%20Necrobloom.op002", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "8957cfa70a1c0088a9fcc3468a316a8ba4ddf6303d982be55406f9e41d676bb1", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--c1e5473fdd48.md and --72afdcd2fb9f (2c tail, 2d); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. claude:mtg 2c/2d are in its 92QA prose (two dredges, second may return a milled land; needs >=2 cards, 702.52b).", "oracle_id": "b981af39-4ee6-4fbc-9a89-618dcad9dfbf", "oracle_text_sha256": "1d25c2af5439699d977cab605396630d6bcee1988be76807233ac201fc1bc49e", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "10a9991f8d2a98fa635a7f703d5f79b0f316c17274e6afc4efc31851d943089b", "question": "Granted dredge 2: which draws can it replace, while what is on the battlefield and in the graveyard, can two lands each dredge into a draw-two (the second returning a land the first milled), and what library size does it need?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["702.52a", "702.52b", "113.6", "614.4", "121.2", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Granted dredge 2 replaces any draw, including draws from triggered abilities and each draw of a draw-N effect (702.52a; 121.2), while The Necrobloom is on the battlefield (113.6) and the land card is in the graveyard (702.52a); the grant ends when The Necrobloom leaves and a replacement must exist before the draw (614.4)."}, {"cr_citations": ["121.2", "702.52a", "702.52b", "113.6", "614.1a", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Any individual draw (121.2, 702.52a), not only the draw step. The grant needs The Necrobloom on the battlefield (113.6) and the land in the graveyard, and ends when The Necrobloom leaves. A draw-two is two draws: two lands may each dredge, and a land milled by the first is eligible for the second if the library still holds at least two cards. Dredge 2 needs at least two cards in library; with fewer it cannot be used."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Auntie Ool, Cursewretch", "contract_id": "card.Auntie%20Ool%2C%20Cursewretch.op002", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "e6bca929148d844dbc550e6a8fce7ce1cfe7dfa7e09aea22af340cf6632306b5", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--a589e410c218.md and --72afdcd2fb9f (3c); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. Refinement from Kate, not a disagreement: claude:mtg's 3c did not say who pays blight or that paying it triggers op002. The representation question (A3 per_event_batch) is its own needs-zach row.", "oracle_id": "e3cd53c1-86bd-4177-adb0-a1fa693b44c6", "oracle_text_sha256": "cea88a292357e0828d49fc7151bc6e7a6aa90d941af135a5a1890d775c27ff07", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "8957cfa70a1c0088a9fcc3468a316a8ba4ddf6303d982be55406f9e41d676bb1", "question": "One event puts -1/-1 counters on several creatures: once or once per creature? Is \"if you control that creature\" checked on resolution, and what if the creature has left? What is Ward—Blight 2 and does paying it trigger her second ability?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "603.4", "608.2c", "608.2h", "702.21a", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Triggers once per creature that receives one or more -1/-1 counters in an event, not once per event (603.2c). 'If you control that creature' is an effect-internal condition checked on resolution (608.2c), using last known information if the creature has left (608.2h). Ward—Blight 2 is a triggered ability with a cost (702.21a) and has no KB contract."}, {"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "603.4", "608.2h", "702.21a", "118.11", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Once per creature that gets one or more -1/-1 counters, however many counters (603.2c). Control is checked on resolution, with last known information if the creature has left (603.4, 608.2h). Ward is a triggered ability that counters the targeting spell or ability unless its controller pays; with the blight reminder text supplied, that opponent puts two -1/-1 counters on a creature they control, which triggers her second ability once, so that opponent ordinarily loses 1 life.", "uncertainty": "medium on blight: no blight-specific CR or ruling in hand"}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Auntie Ool, Cursewretch", "contract_id": "card.Auntie%20Ool%2C%20Cursewretch.op002", "disagreement_type": "ontology_representation", "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "f9c1dfc391133e29eccd4e2093d22d6eff3bf946975c79cd7075f498d573588e", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "dio_representation", "notes": "Kate did not address the KB representation (her ask carried no KB state, by design). The mechanics reading behind it is the agreed row for this contract. Round 10 (Saga lore counters crossing several chapters in one put) raises the same cardinality question from the other side.", "oracle_id": "e3cd53c1-86bd-4177-adb0-a1fa693b44c6", "oracle_text_sha256": "cea88a292357e0828d49fc7151bc6e7a6aa90d941af135a5a1890d775c27ff07", "outcome": "needs-zach", "prev": "e6bca929148d844dbc550e6a8fce7ce1cfe7dfa7e09aea22af340cf6632306b5", "question": "Representation: the KB records the op002 hook as counter.put, cardinality one_or_more, simultaneity_group per_event_batch (DIO addendum A3). Both readers say the ability fires once per creature in an event. Does A3 need a per-object-in-batch cardinality?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "A3's one_or_more + per_event_batch counts one firing per event; the rules give one firing per creature per event (603.2c). The correct shape is a per-object-in-batch cardinality, which A3 lacks. Changing it is a dio_revision-adjacent decision (P-09), so this is Zach's call, not a reading."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Tidus, Yuna's Guardian", "contract_id": "card.Tidus%2C%20Yuna's%20Guardian.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "c9e5e52f943be1e3bbc81a169f5ecc7bc55a5b35c985f575eb8448717894cf54", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--72afdcd2fb9f.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. claude:mtg marked 4b as its least certain claim; Kate answered it with high confidence and the same direction, so the row is agreed. Neither side cited a dated ruling; a Hardened Scales ruling (Kate, from memory) is the evidence to fetch before any review.", "oracle_id": "e8fbcafd-3617-4cd7-b55d-457fb7b60162", "oracle_text_sha256": "529df1b6945b94fe7b292ecf078d59a0ed2892b9e946d8365eb9fcc6f8fa5e87", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "f9c1dfc391133e29eccd4e2093d22d6eff3bf946975c79cd7075f498d573588e", "question": "Moving a counter: is it a counter \"put on\" the receiving creature (so Auntie Ool's op002 triggers)? Do would-be-put replacement effects apply to the moved counter? What happens with no counter to move, an illegal target, or the same creature chosen twice?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["122.5", "122.6", "115.3", "608.2b", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Moving a counter removes it from the first object and puts it onto the second (122.5); the put half is a counter being put on a creature (122.6), so 'whenever one or more counters are put on' listeners trigger. If either half is impossible, including the same creature as both targets (115.3), nothing moves (122.5). Whether would-be-put replacement effects modify a moved counter is my least certain claim."}, {"cr_citations": ["122.5", "614.1", "608.2b", "601.2c", "603.3d", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Yes: moving is removing from the first and putting on the second (122.5), so a moved -1/-1 counter triggers Ool. Replacement effects modify the put half (614.1), possibly increasing what arrives without increasing what leaves; Hardened Scales itself only touches +1/+1 counters. No counter to move, or either target illegal: nothing moves (the ability still resolves if one target is legal; 608.2b). 'A second target' needs a different creature, so the same creature twice is not a legal choice.", "uncertainty": "medium-high on the distinct-target wording"}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Evolution Sage", "contract_id": "card.Evolution%20Sage.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "4d6535360fdc27615e606e9c30a46668111cfdc7736adcac6ec47a6627eca9b8", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--293666839b50.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition.", "oracle_id": "b45fdeab-00cc-4422-af9f-66f30a880a7c", "oracle_text_sha256": "483dd6e9c6ba22a4e307b123ea5adecebb0ffc584e2d09a38ca204065eeb8c60", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "c9e5e52f943be1e3bbc81a169f5ecc7bc55a5b35c985f575eb8448717894cf54", "question": "Proliferate (via Evolution Sage, and Tidus's Cheer): is it a counters-put event per chosen object, can you choose zero or only some, does it add new kinds, and does Cheer's 'only once each turn' limit the trigger or the effect?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["701.27a", "122.6", "603.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Proliferate puts one additional counter of each kind already present on each chosen permanent or player (701.27a); each is a counter put on that object (122.6), so per-creature listeners trigger once per chosen creature (603.2c). Any number includes zero and may be only your own permanents. 'Do this only once each turn' limits the effect, not the trigger (603.2c), and declining the may does not spend it."}, {"cr_citations": ["701.27a", "122.6", "603.2c", "608.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Proliferate puts counters, one of each kind already there (701.27a, 122.6), so Ool triggers once per chosen creature (603.2c). You may choose zero or any subset. No new kinds. Cheer's limit is on the effect; declining the may does not spend it."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Leonardo, the Balance", "contract_id": "card.Leonardo%2C%20the%20Balance.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "98539b396f233e7eb59658a57b78c2cb0a89cb7122c29164fa7dafe68b2b9f7b", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--293666839b50.md and --4b7951b9638c (6c); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition.", "oracle_id": "46ea8d02-b087-44f7-8403-93ffc1d3a8ad", "oracle_text_sha256": "be5d0cf59e5ab3d00dce36deec37065fae220e7372f566b701e32d76960ebf54", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "4d6535360fdc27615e606e9c30a46668111cfdc7736adcac6ec47a6627eca9b8", "question": "Three tokens enter at once: three triggers? Is 'do this only once each turn' a limit on the trigger or the effect, does declining spend it, and does 'each turn' renew on every player's turn?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "603.3", "608.2h", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "One trigger per token entering, even when several enter in one event (603.2c). 'Do this only once each turn' limits the effect, not the trigger: every trigger resolves, the first one you accept puts the counters (608.2h counts creatures on resolution), and declining does not spend the once. 'Each turn' renews on every player's turn. The KB contract's capacity entry already represents this; the block is C11."}, {"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "500.1", "603.2", "608.2c", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Three triggers (603.2c). The limit is on the effect; declining the optional counters does not use the turn's allowance. 'Each turn' means every turn, opponents' included."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Rootha, Mastering the Moment", "contract_id": "card.Rootha%2C%20Mastering%20the%20Moment.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "3809d6da4f5c8ce51e6b5a7260ac52f8f7a5f6a97417b884efa6191b72f6e7e2", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--76b356089134.md and --4b7951b9638c (7c citations); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. Refinement from Kate: claude:mtg's 'copies are not cast' omits copies an effect tells you to cast (707.12). Candidate rewording for any review: 'a copy put on the stack is not cast; a copy you are told to cast is'.", "oracle_id": "348c67ef-9ccc-4651-9038-efdf1ad1b36a", "oracle_text_sha256": "6a066099b726b64ce0b50485d404c45666d50756645a6db2b83d41d4714bdaf9", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "98539b396f233e7eb59658a57b78c2cb0a89cb7122c29164fa7dafe68b2b9f7b", "question": "Is the cast condition an intervening if? When is X fixed? Do spells cast before Rootha entered, copies of spells, and spells cast from exile or a graveyard count?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["603.4", "608.2h", "707.10", "601.2", "202.3b", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Intervening if (603.4): checked as combat begins and on resolution; no trigger if no instant or sorcery was cast this turn. X is fixed as the ability resolves (608.2h) and the token does not change size later. Spells cast earlier in the turn count regardless of when Rootha entered; copies of spells are not cast (707.10) and count for neither the condition nor X; casting from exile or a graveyard counts."}, {"cr_citations": ["603.4", "608.2h", "601.2", "707.10", "707.12", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Intervening if, checked when combat begins and on resolution (603.4); X fixed on resolution (608.2h). Earlier casts this turn count, and casting from exile or a graveyard is casting (601.2). A copy merely put on the stack is not cast (707.10), but a copy a player is instructed to cast goes through casting and is cast (707.12, 601.2)."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Ashling, the Limitless", "contract_id": "card.Ashling%2C%20the%20Limitless.op002", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "5c0f75ab25848d82e1a8496cdf6cb83c3ae3e595a6ee488c76e2b9912206ced8", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--4b7951b9638c.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. KB gap (claude:mtg, unchanged): op003 is the delayed trigger op002 creates, not an independent ability.", "oracle_id": "77a9e7cf-76e9-4323-8504-a5b831de00be", "oracle_text_sha256": "a450abb07280480004ad3f5a9e11d1e90c6efadd9cd69676f20d0ae45729c4fb", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "3809d6da4f5c8ce51e6b5a7260ac52f8f7a5f6a97417b884efa6191b72f6e7e2", "question": "What does the token copy (graveyard card or the permanent as it last existed; counters, Auras, copy effects)? Is the end-step sacrifice a delayed trigger tracking that token? Does sacrificing the token, or Ashling herself, trigger her?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["707.2", "608.2h", "603.7a", "603.7b", "603.7c", "603.10a", "603.6a", "702.74", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "The token copies the sacrificed Elemental's copiable values as it last existed on the battlefield (707.2, 608.2h): copy effects yes, counters and Auras no. The end-step sacrifice is a delayed triggered ability created by the same ability's resolution (603.7a-c), tracking that token only; paying {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} keeps it. The token's own sacrifice does not re-trigger (nontoken); sacrificing Ashling does, via look-back (603.10a)."}, {"cr_citations": ["608.2h", "707.2", "603.7", "603.7c", "400.7", "111.8", "603.10a", "701.17", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "The permanent as it last existed on the battlefield (608.2h): copiable values, including an applicable copy effect (707.2); not counters, Auras or their ordinary modifications. The end-step sacrifice is a delayed triggered ability (603.7); a token that leaves cannot return, and a returned object would be new (400.7, 111.8). Sacrificing the token does not trigger (it is a token); sacrificing Ashling does, by look-back (603.10a)."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Amalia Benavides Aguirre", "contract_id": "card.Amalia%20Benavides%20Aguirre.op002", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "2ed1af0aabbb6d264f6e625b4d703cf743e3dff5ff79918622363ee552d4b8fa", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--ad8cef3c55e3.md and --4b7951b9638c (9c); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. Inconsistency on claude:mtg's own side, found in this comparison: its 9c prose says an empty library does not stop the loop (agreeing with Kate), but its writer-ready summary says the loop 'ends only at exactly 20 or an empty library'. The prose is the reading; the summary sentence is wrong. Refinement from Kate: the pending Walker trigger after the wipe.", "oracle_id": "85eefda9-4aab-467d-a08c-be026cb8ff42", "oracle_text_sha256": "1e404cd99daccdaa717225cf33b1db57bbb7c0a3be63dd3043381cfa920d3943", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "5c0f75ab25848d82e1a8496cdf6cb83c3ae3e595a6ee488c76e2b9912206ced8", "question": "One explore per life-gain event, power checked after the explore on resolution? Who survives the wipe? With a Wildgrowth Walker-style loop: mandatory, how it ends, power skipping 20, a land reveal, an empty library?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["603.2c", "603.4", "608.2c", "608.2h", "701.40a", "701.40b", "701.40c", "701.7a", "701.7c", "702.12b", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "One trigger per life-gain event (603.2c). Amalia explores first (701.40a), then 'if its power is exactly 20' is checked as the effect reaches it on resolution (608.2c), after any counter from the explore; LKI applies if she has left (701.40c, 608.2h). 'Other' excludes her; indestructible and regeneration survive (702.12b, 701.7c). The Walker loop is mandatory and ends only at exactly 20 or an empty library; skipping 20 makes a mandatory, unstoppable loop (draw under Taking Shortcuts). Role: a lifegain grower with a conditional wipe; whether it counts as a wipe for coverage is Zach's."}, {"cr_citations": ["603.2", "603.4", "608.2c", "701.7", "702.12", "701.40", "104.4b", "113.7a", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "One trigger per life-gain event; power is checked after the explore on resolution (608.2c); 'other' excludes Amalia; indestructible survives and regeneration applies. The Walker loop is mandatory and ends when a resolution finds power exactly 20 and the wipe destroys the Walker; if power passes 20 and cannot return, the unbreakable loop is a draw (104.4b). A land reveal still counts as exploring, so the Walker still triggers; an empty library does not stop it (exploring is not drawing). A Walker trigger already on the stack still resolves after the wipe (113.7a), giving one more explore."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Amalia Benavides Aguirre", "contract_id": "card.Amalia%20Benavides%20Aguirre.op002", "disagreement_type": "contextual_role", "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "294afc01c33d5bae218067e428cb27288c17cef8ab98038940ea3b5a46c2bc21", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "deck_role", "notes": "Both readers give the same opinion; it is an intent question, so the row is needs-zach whatever they say. kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--4b7951b9638c.md.", "oracle_id": "85eefda9-4aab-467d-a08c-be026cb8ff42", "oracle_text_sha256": "1e404cd99daccdaa717225cf33b1db57bbb7c0a3be63dd3043381cfa920d3943", "outcome": "needs-zach", "prev": "2ed1af0aabbb6d264f6e625b4d703cf743e3dff5ff79918622363ee552d4b8fa", "question": "Should the KB / evaluator count Amalia as a board wipe, a life-gain payoff that grows, or both under a condition (C-012; DEC-130 Yin/Yang coverage counts)?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Both: role payoff(lifegain) with counter.put +1/+1, and role wipe qualified by power == 20 on resolution; the evaluator should never present the wipe unqualified. Whether it counts as a wipe for coverage is Zach's.", "uncertainty": "intent, not rules"}, {"cr_citations": ["oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Opinion, intent question: both, conditionally; a life-gain payoff that grows, tagged separately as a conditional exact-20 creature wipe, not an unconditional board wipe.", "uncertainty": "labelled opinion by Kate"}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Terra, Magical Adept // Esper Terra", "contract_id": "card.Terra%2C%20Magical%20Adept%20%2F%2F%20Esper%20Terra.op006", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "f10e548212aeb786bd52dfe9f1f9f0ca9f6d0e5303899e05277c2168024011e2", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--4182d31467b2.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. Same substance on 10b, put differently: claude:mtg says the SBA pre-empts the end-step sacrifice \"almost always\" (whenever the counters reach the final chapter); Kate says neither has unconditional priority and gives the same condition. KB gaps (claude:mtg, unchanged): op006 lacks haste and the delayed sacrifice; op003/op007 record from: graveyard where the zone is exile.", "oracle_id": "54ca5904-9099-497a-9684-101656025487", "oracle_text_sha256": "fa63b419460cb6159032445563678b5f92faddc97ab7cf83e0ef1e65e242f9c3", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "294afc01c33d5bae218067e428cb27288c17cef8ab98038940ea3b5a46c2bc21", "question": "A token copy of a Saga: lore counter on entry, which chapters trigger when 'up to three' go on at once, which sacrifice comes first, can you put fewer, who orders the chapters; after Trance and after chapter IV, what triggers again?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["714.2b", "714.2c", "714.3a", "714.3b", "714.4", "603.3", "603.3b", "603.6d", "603.7a", "603.7c", "400.7", "707.2", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "A token copy of a Saga enters with a lore counter (714.3a), triggering chapter I (714.2b). Terra's 'up to three' counters are one event, so every chapter whose threshold is crossed triggers at once (714.2b), in the controller's chosen stack order (603.3b). Once lore >= final chapter and no chapter ability is on the stack, the state-based action sacrifices the token (714.4), pre-empting Terra's end-step delayed trigger (603.7a, 603.7c); putting fewer counters keeps the token to the end step. Trance and chapter IV each return a new object (400.7): chapter I and the ETB mill trigger again."}, {"cr_citations": ["707.2", "714.3a", "714.2b", "714.2c", "714.4", "704.3", "603.7", "603.3b", "608.2d", "400.7", "712.14", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "The token enters with a lore counter and chapter I triggers (714.3a); adding three in one event triggers every chapter crossed (714.2b-c). The Saga SBA sacrifices it once lore reaches the final chapter and no chapter ability is pending (714.4); otherwise Terra's delayed trigger at your next end step does (603.7). 'Up to three' allows fewer, which postpones the SBA but not the end-step sacrifice; the controller orders simultaneous chapter triggers (603.3b). Trance and chapter IV each return a new object (400.7): chapter I, and later Terra's enters mill, trigger again."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Silvergill Peddler", "contract_id": "card.Silvergill%20Peddler.op001", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "b86c74f685c1f38043e849887401078a5531b281cc49c964a272df0f5e98537c", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--eda016006f9f.md; the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. claude:mtg's reading is a compaction of its 92QA round 11 prose and scenarios (no writer-ready JSON was written for round 11). 11d (convoke tapping is not tapping for mana) is Kate's only: one voice, recorded here as context, not agreed.", "oracle_id": "08688903-d9cc-4d57-ba91-14a8523551b9", "oracle_text_sha256": "e0813430a2354a3a2de358b91137b017bbcb989f99798169b8d10f0f44314c4a", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "f10e548212aeb786bd52dfe9f1f9f0ca9f6d0e5303899e05277c2168024011e2", "question": "Tapping Silvergill Peddler to pay convoke for Merrow Skyswimmer: does it 'become tapped' for its own trigger, when does the loot resolve relative to Skyswimmer, and what if Skyswimmer is countered?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["702.51a", "603.2a", "603.3", "601.2i", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Yes. Convoke is paid by tapping creatures while casting (702.51a); a creature tapped as a cost has become tapped and its trigger fires (603.2a). The trigger goes on the stack the next time a player would receive priority, after Skyswimmer is cast, so the loot resolves first (603.3, 601.2i). If Skyswimmer is countered the loot still happens: the cost was paid."}, {"cr_citations": ["702.51a", "702.51b", "603.2", "601.2i", "603.3", "113.7a", "106.12", "605.1a", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Peddler triggers when tapped for convoke (702.51a-b, 603.2). The trigger waits until casting completes, goes on the stack above Skyswimmer and resolves first (601.2i, 603.3). It still happens if Skyswimmer is countered (113.7a). Deepchannel Duelist untapping it lets it convoke again later; tapping for convoke is not tapping for mana (106.12, 605.1a)."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Sharuum the Hegemon", "contract_id": "card.Sharuum%20the%20Hegemon.op002", "disagreement_type": null, "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "2a89b8f98baf2d5c1f8388b4c8f1ce22bda6f970bc9770da1d4be8b3eb106553", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "mechanics", "notes": "Paired independent first readings (92QA Part 2 option 2, Zach 2026-11-15 \"5, 2\"): claude:mtg wrote its side 2026-11-07..09 in outputs/HO-MTG-20261107-92QA.md; Kate (API instance, ask-only, redacted context: questions and Oracle text only) answered 2026-11-15. Kate's text here is claude:mtg's summary of kate-replies (relay-kit-private branch) replies/HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q--eda016006f9f.md and --4182d31467b2 (12b citations, 12c, 12d); the reply file is the verbatim record. CR numbers on both sides are from memory, unchecked against a 2026 edition. 12d (copies) is Kate's only: a copy of Sharuum has and triggers the return ability, referring to the copy. Her aside that the ability 'contains no self-name reference' contradicts her own 12a (201.5): 'When Sharuum enters' is one. Her conclusion is unaffected. claude:mtg's reading is a compaction of its 92QA round 12 prose.", "oracle_id": "037e7fc9-3aa6-484c-a2c8-43009e45f1d8", "oracle_text_sha256": "0eb65e978ca40346ac6bb4e5267eadd798bb6d0296208b6510dfd9b2c2764374", "outcome": "agreed", "prev": "b86c74f685c1f38043e849887401078a5531b281cc49c964a272df0f5e98537c", "question": "'When Sharuum enters': self only? When are the target and the 'may' decided, what if there is no legal target, and what if the targeted card leaves the graveyard before resolution?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["201.5", "603.3d", "608.2c", "608.2b", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "Self only: a card's own name in its text means that object (201.5). The target is chosen when the trigger is put on the stack (603.3d); 'you may' is decided on resolution (608.2c). If the targeted card leaves the graveyard first, the ability does nothing (608.2b)."}, {"cr_citations": ["201.5", "603.6a", "603.3d", "601.2c", "603.5", "608.2d", "608.2b", "400.7", "oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "gpt-6.1-sol", "party": "kate", "reading": "Self only (201.5, 603.6a). Target chosen as the ability is put on the stack, the optional return decided on resolution (603.3d, 601.2c, 603.5, 608.2d); with no legal target it is removed from the stack. If the target leaves the graveyard the ability has no legal target and does not resolve; a card that comes back is a new object (608.2b, 400.7)."}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
{"card_or_mechanic": "Sharuum the Hegemon", "contract_id": "card.Sharuum%20the%20Hegemon.op002", "disagreement_type": "insufficient_evidence", "in_kb": true, "interpretation_id": "3ebcccc24800eb2d2994e8ef2fb7b251a691db75be4db172a152a1de0add3e0c", "kb_release": "mtg-kb-v0.2.1-r20261104", "layer": "deck_role", "notes": "Not asked of Kate: a deck-role question with no rules content. Opened so the question is on record beside the mechanics row.", "oracle_id": "037e7fc9-3aa6-484c-a2c8-43009e45f1d8", "oracle_text_sha256": "0eb65e978ca40346ac6bb4e5267eadd798bb6d0296208b6510dfd9b2c2764374", "outcome": "needs-zach", "prev": "2a89b8f98baf2d5c1f8388b4c8f1ce22bda6f970bc9770da1d4be8b3eb106553", "question": "Q18 swap in the Sharuum deck: which swap did the evaluator prefer, which did Zach make, and why?", "readings": [{"cr_citations": ["oracle"], "independent": true, "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "party": "claude:mtg", "reading": "No record readable by this lane names the two cards or the reason. The row can only ask Zach for them: decision provenance (CHARTER 6).", "uncertainty": "no evidence in any record"}], "recorded_by": "claude:mtg#wake-20261115-23", "scenarios": null, "source": "HO-MTG-20261115-C20Q", "subject_kind": "card", "supersedes": null, "utc": "2026-11-15T23:52:46+00:00", "verification_state": "candidate"}
